<title>FRANCE: L'Oreal 1996 sales 60.34 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>L'Oreal 1996 sales 60.34 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(All figures in billions of French francs)</p>
<p>Turnover					60.34     vs   53.37</p>
<p>NOTE - L'Oreal said in a statement that its annual sales were up 13 percent from 1995 levels.</p>
<p>Its consolidated cosmetics sales grew by 13.2 percent, and sales for its Synthelabo subsidiary rose 12.4 percent.</p>
<p>It said its acquisitions Jade in Germany and Interbeauty in Israel have been consolidated into the group since January 1, 1996. Its U.S. acquisition Maybelline was consolidated into the group as of February 12, 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;On a directly comparable basis, based on identical group structure and exchange rates, consolidated sales for L'Oreal in 1996 increased by eight percent,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
